<title>CYPRUS: Cyprus Trading 96 turnover up 32pct.</title>
<headline>Cyprus Trading 96 turnover up 32pct.</headline>
<text>
<p>NICOSIA, April 21 - Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		  (In thousands of pounds unless stated)</p>
<p>						  1996	 1995</p>
<p>    Turnover				61,319	46,463</p>
<p>Profit before depreciation and</p>
<p>    interest				 4,926	 2,980</p>
<p>    Depreciation			     945	   404</p>
<p>    Interest				 1,734	   795</p>
<p>    Profit from operations	     2,247	 1,781</p>
<p>Share of profit of associated</p>
<p>    company				    317	   322</p>
<p>Profit before amortisation of</p>
<p>    goodwill				 2,564	 2,103</p>
<p>    Amortisation of goodwill	     357	    43</p>
<p>    Profit before exceptional item   2,207	 2,060</p>
<p>    Exceptional item			 -	   1,349</p>
<p>    Profit before taxation	     2,207	 3,409</p>
<p>    Taxation				   521	   455</p>
<p>    Profit after taxation		1,685	 2,953</p>
<p>    Minority interest			 99	    22</p>
<p>Profit attributable to</p>
<p>    shareholders			   1,586	 2,931</p>
<p>Proposed dividend (7%, 7 cents</p>
<p>    per share)			     1,137	    --</p>
<p>Profit transferred to revenue</p>
<p>    reserve				    449	 2,931</p>
<p>    Basic earnings per share (cents)*     9.77    19.45</p>
<p>    EPS before exceptional item (cents)* 13.59    13.67</p>
<p>    Fully diluted EPS (cents)*		9.74</p>
<p>Note: Full company name is Cyprus Trading Corporation Limited (CTC). It holds dealerships in Cyprus for Philips Electronics luxury carmaker Saab and Scania heavy machinery, as well as controlling stakes in a number of local firms.</p>
<p>The exceptional item relates to the sale of Lemeco textiles in 1995.</p>
<p>* The results are preliminary and unaudited</p>
<p>* Earnings per share for 1995 have been restated due to the issue of bonus shares in 1996</p>
<p>* Earnings per share have been diluted due to the issue of the convertible debenture loan in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Nicosia newsroom 357 2 365089</p>
</text>
